    "title" : "PicoLOOP - LAUV Circumnavigation of Pico Island to Demonstrate Remote Robotic Operations During C3-4OCEAN Activities",
    "summary": "A mission involving the deployment of two Light Autonomous Underwater Vehicles (LAUVs) was conducted as part of the WHISTLE (Western Iberian Shelf Integrated Multimodel Forecast Service for Transnational Environmental Management) use case, supported by the Copernicus Marine Service National Collaboration Programme (2022–2028). The operation employed two LAUVs owned by the University of Porto, each equipped with CTD sensors, to survey coastal waters influenced by the Douro, Ave, and Cávado rivers. The vehicles performed vertical profiling (“yoyo dives”) down to 100m depth, covering trajectories of approximately 130 km over 40–50 hours, consisting of two transects perpendicular to the coast and one parallel. A 4–6 hour time lag between the two LAUVs was maintained to capture transient temperature and salinity variations. Minor trajectory anomalies were observed when the vehicles exceeded the pre-set maximum operating depth.",
    "keywords": "temperature of the water column \u2013 TEMP \u2013 WC_Temp; salinity of the water column \u2013 PSAL \u2013 WC_Sal; electrical conductivity of the water column \u2013 CNDC \u2013 WC_Cond; sound velocity in the water column \u2013 SVEL \u2013 WC_SoundVel; ",
    "project_uri": "https://nowsystems.eu/en/project-nologin-oceanic-weather-WHISTLE",
    "keywords_vocabulary": "SeaDataNet parameter discovery vocabulary ",
    "project": "Marine Robotics Summer School",
    "QC_indicator": "The data provided here was filterered through a quality control process that imports specific tests from IOOS' \"Manual for Real-Time Quality Control of In-situ Temperature and Salinity Data\", specifically: \n 1) All salinty and temperature was limited to values between 15 and 40 and 8 and 30, respectively. \n 2) All values were filtered using a rolling-window method that calculates the average value of three sequenced measurements (n-1, n, n+1) in order to create a reference value. Each value in the center of this rolling window is compared with this reference, |VAL_ref - VAL_n| to detect measurement spikes. If this difference computes a value higher than 4, then VAL_n is discarded from the measurements. This applies to both temeperature and salinity data. Same threshold was used",
    "principal_investigator": "Jo\u00e3o Borges de Sousa",
    "principal_investigator_email": "jtasso@fe.up.pt",
    "license": "CC-BY"
}


